  "seoTitle": "PT Fonusa Agung Mulia Fire Investigation Update",
  "metaDescription": "Authorities have identified twenty-five victims of the PT Fonusa Agung Mulia factory fire in Cikande as the investigation into potential negligence continues.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Disaster Victim Identification teams have successfully identified twenty-five individuals among the victims of the factory fire.",
    "Police have officially upgraded the case to a formal investigation due to suspected workplace safety violations.",
    "Ongoing search efforts are being hampered by the structural instability of the facility, which remains at risk of collapse."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "A major fire occurred at the PT Fonusa Agung Mulia candy factory located in Cikande, Serang. Recovery efforts have resulted in the collection of twenty-six body bags to date, with twenty-five victims confirmed via identification processes. The disaster has prompted significant scrutiny regarding workplace health and safety standards. Union leader Said Iqbal has suggested that the facility may have violated established safety regulations and requested that the company provide compensation of one billion rupiah to the families of the deceased. Meanwhile, local law enforcement has elevated the case to a formal investigation phase, citing findings of potential negligence. Search operations at the site are currently restricted as structural experts have deemed the remaining factory architecture unsafe for entry, complicating the recovery of additional remains.",
